 "title": "Clearing Control in Incoming Payments",
 "cover_area_title": null,
 "raw_text": "9/29/26, 9:49 AM\n\nClearing Control in Incoming Payments\n\nDuring the processing of externally initiated payments, the system attempts in event 0110 to assign the payment amount to the\n\nopen items. By default, the system posts unassigned amounts and partial amounts of a payment on account.\n\nClearing control takes account of entries in the same fields, as in account maintenance. Additional postings, such as payments on\n\naccount and expense and revenue postings, can also be set up.\n\nee Example\n\nA payment of 50- is received.\n\nHVORG\n\nPayable Amount\n\nTVORG\n\n50                           Clearing Proposal\n\nXAKTP           AUGBW\n\nInvoice\n\nReceivable\n\nInvoice\n\nReceivable\n\nOn Account\n\nCredit\n\nBudget\nBilling\nAmount\n\nClearing Control in Incoming Payments\n\nReceivable\n\nOn Account\n\nE_DIFFB     | 0 |\n| -10 |\n",
